ff documents on file with the California Public Utilities Commission.\n\nIf I have questions on my results or how to use this file, I should contact my billing representative at 1-800-427-5776.\n\nDownload the MHP Calculator\n\n(Note on Security Settings: If prompted, you need to \"Enable Macros.\")\n\n## Safety Services For Customers with Sub-Metered Natural Gas Service\n\n  * Safety Brochure - English (PDF)\n  * Safety Brochure - Español (PDF)\n\n## Related Information\n\nYou need the Adobe Acrobat Reader to view these documents.\n\nRates and Schedules\n\n  * GR\n  * G-CARE\n  * G-PPPS\n  * G-SRF\n  * G-MHPS\n  * G-TCA\n\nRules\n\n  * Rule No. 24\n\nMonthly Billing Factors\n\nBTU Districts and Monthly Billing Factor--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisconnections Proceeding – Arrearage Management Plan Advice Letter - California Choice Energy Authority (https://californiachoiceenergyauthority.com/disconnections-proceeding-arrearage-management-plan-advice-letter/)\nciteturn1436search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.0 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; On July 20, 2018, the CPUC issued Rulemaking (R.) 18-07-005 to implement the requirements of SB 598 in order to address disconnection rates across California’s electric IOUs by adopting policies and rules that reduce disconnections and improve reconnections processes and outcomes for disconnected customers. ... Decision (D.) 20-06-003 (the Decision) ordered IOUs to submit Advice Letters within 90 days of the effective date to establish an Arrearage Management Plan (AMP).\n\n# Disconnections Proceeding – Arrearage Management Plan Advice Letter\n\nClick here to view the document.\n\n### Description\n\nOn July 20, 2018, the CPUC issued Rulemaking (R.) 18-07-005 to implement the requirements of SB 598 in order to address disconnection rates across California’s electric IOUs by adopting policies and rules that reduce disconnections and improve reconnections processes and outcomes for disconnected customers. As part of the Rulemaking, on June 16, 2020, the CPUC issued another decision adopting rules designed to reduce the number of residential customer disconnections.\n\nDecision (D.) 20-06-003 (the Decision) ordered IOUs to submit Advice Letters within 90 days of the effective date to establish an Arrearage Management Plan (AMP). The Decision requires that AMP be designed to forgive 1/12 of a customer’s total arrearage each month in exchange for the customer making on-time payments on their current bill. The customer would effectively have all arrears forgiven after one year of on-time payments. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOperadores de complejos residenciales y parques de casas rodantes | SoCalGas (https://www.socalgas.com/es/billing-payment/understanding-my-bill/mhp)\nciteturn1436search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; Crawled: last month; La Calculadora de Factura de SoCalGas® le permite calcular la factura de gas mensual individual de un inquilino que utilice un submedidor de gas. ...   * Rule No.24\nSe me ha recomendado verificar los cálculos con la documentación sobre tarifas autorizada que figura en los registros de la Comisión de Servicios Públicos de California (California Public Utilities Commission, CPUC).\n\nSi tengo preguntas sobre los resultados o sobre cómo usar este archivo, deberé ponerme en contacto con el representante de facturación que me corresponda al 1-800-427-5776.\n\nDescargar la calculadora MHP\n\n(Nota sobre la configuración de seguridad: Si se le solicita, necesita \"Activar Macros (Enable Macros).\")\n\n## Servicios de seguridad para clientes con submedidores de gas natural\n\n  * Folleto de seguridad 2015 - en inglés (PDF)\n  * Folleto de seguridad 2015 - en español (PDF)\n\n## Información relacionad\n\nEs necesario contar con Adobe Acrobat Reader para ver estos documentos.\n\nCuadro tarifario\n\n  * GR\n  * G-CARE\n  * G-PPPS\n  * G-SRF\n  * 